# Keep the build context to the runtime payload. Two entries here are correctness, not size:
#
#  * projects/ and .app-state/ are the LIVE DATA STORES on the dev machine (git-backed reading
#    projects, API keys in settings.json, a multi-GB audio cache). Baking them into an image would
#    ship real keys into a registry and would shadow the mounted volume at /data. Never include.
#  * .env holds secrets. Production config comes from `fly secrets`, never from a file in the image.

.git
.gitignore
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Live data + secrets — see above.
projects/
project/
.app-state/
.env

# Not part of the server runtime.
tests/
mobile/
scripts/
docs/
shared/
.github/
.claude/
web/node_modules/
web/src/
web/public/
*.md
run.sh
tunnel.sh
